From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:01:41 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] FLEET: Upstream sync 2026-11-10 entry, regenerated patch
 mirror, refreshed flag checklist

Writes up the 36e36e63a..202c1a229 merge (433 upstream commits), every conflict resolution and
the three post-merge regressions ctest caught outside any conflict marker. Regenerates
fleet-patches/*.patch (345 -> 347, BASE=202c1a229f5a83d1c9d758ed0f2d43760fa4bab0, no EXCLUDE, same
convention as the 2026-11-04 mirror) and the BASE/EXCLUDE note in the "Fleet patch maintenance"
section.

Also replaces the Upstream-sync compatibility checklist's item 5 flag list with one actually
extracted from home-infrastructure's values*.yaml/templates: the command recorded there used
`rg -h`, which in ripgrep 14 means "show help" (not "no filename" as in older rg/grep), so the
previous list was never drawn from the fleet's real files. Re-extracted with `rg -oNI` and
confirmed every flag against the new llama-server --help.

