+From 7571530fa7ee35f913b9d67be887062f9a1ea08b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
+Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:50:24 -0600
+Subject: [PATCH] Restore the fork's concat-free conv-state store, fix three
+ more merge regressions
+
+Found by running ctest on the 2026-11-10 upstream merge:
+
+- delta-net-base.cpp / qwen4exp.cpp: the merge had swapped the fork's per-slot conv-window stores for upstream's build_conv_state_store(). That helper expects conv_x to be the materialized concat(history, tokens); the fork's build_conv_state/_split deliberately return {prefix, new_tokens} for ggml_ssm_conv_split and never build the concat, so the helper cut views out of a transposed tensor and hit the new GGML_ASSERT in ggml_view_impl (test-state-capture). Back to build_conv_window()/build_token_cols() as before the merge.
+- peg-parser.cpp: upstream's recursion limit indexes ctx.rule_depth, which only the root parse() sizes. The K2-Horizon lenient-fallback parse in chat.cpp starts at a rule on a fresh context, so rule_depth was empty and test-chat segfaulted. The rule parser now grows rule_depth on demand.
+- test-backend-ops.cpp: test_ssm_conv_split_graph viewed a transposed tensor and patched nb[0] by hand; upstream's view assert (#31584) rejects that. It now cuts the tail from the contiguous rows and transposes, like build_token_cols.
+- test-llama-context.cpp: four model threads load in one process; --split-balance's default (auto) memory probe swaps the same global log callback that fit_params=false already avoids, which crashed the run. The test sets split_balance to memory.
+
+Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet
